<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jajpur</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jajpur is a town on the Baitarani river in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/odisha">Odisha</a>, eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, and headquarters of the district of the same name. It was a capital of the Bhauma-Kara and Somavamshi dynasties and is an important <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hinduism">Hindu</a> pilgrimage centre, with the temple of the goddess Viraja (Biraja). Nearby are the Buddhist sites of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ratnagiri">Ratnagiri</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lalitagiri">Lalitagiri</a> and Udayagiri.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jajpur.jpg" alt="Jajpur" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: SUDEEP PRAMANIK · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ratnagiri_Monastery_,_Jajpur._Odisha.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
